---
title: Migrating to TanStack Table V9 (Vue)
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-s-new-in-tanstack-table-v9","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What's New in TanStack Table V9"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Table V9 delivers major performance improvements, hundreds of bug fixes, new and refreshed features, and optional helpers for composing and managing tables. Despite the scale of the release, the headless model, core table logic, column definitions, and rendering patterns remain familiar. Here are the key changes:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-better-performance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Better Performance"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lower memory usage"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The core architecture now shares more behavior across table objects, with some large-table scenarios seeing up to 90% memory savings."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Faster client-side row models"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Sorting, filtering, and aggregation paths have improved algorithms and memoization, with many scenarios seeing up to 40-70% speed improvements."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Better column resizing performance"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The same architectural and memoization work also speeds up column resizing."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-state-management-overhaul","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. State Management Overhaul"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Store foundation"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Table state is backed by TanStack Store atoms."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue reactivity integration"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Table atoms are backed by Vue refs and computed values, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTable"},{"type":"text","value":" unwraps reactive option values like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fine-grained subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Registered features expose per-slice state through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.atoms"},{"type":"text","value":", so reads can stay scoped to the state they need."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-type-safety-improvements","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Type-Safety Improvements"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New and revamped type helpers"}]},{"type":"text","value":": There are helpers for defining columns, custom filters, sorts, aggregations, column and table meta, shared table options and components, and more."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-table meta types"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" slots let you type meta for a specific table instead of globally augmenting shared interfaces. "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No more global declaration merging required!"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature-gated APIs"}]},{"type":"text","value":": APIs only exist when their feature is registered, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures()"},{"type":"text","value":" validates feature prerequisites at the type level."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"4-tree-shaking-and-extensibility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Tree Shaking and Extensibility"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import only the features you use"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Tables that only need sorting do not ship filtering, pagination, or other unused feature code."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tree-shakeable row models and functions"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Row model factories and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" now live on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures()"},{"type":"text","value":", so unused processing code can be dropped."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom features use the same system"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Your own feature plugins can register state, options, and APIs alongside the built-in features. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./custom-features.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Features Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"5-composability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Composability"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions()"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Compose reusable table configuration, including features, row models, and default options."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook()"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Define shared Vue table factories with pre-bound features, row models, defaults, and components."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"6-new-and-refreshed-features","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6. New and Refreshed Features"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New Features"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell Selection"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cellSelectionFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" adds spreadsheet-style rectangular cell range selection, with drag, Shift-extend, and multiple disjoint ranges. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./cell-selection.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell Selection Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell Spanning"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cellSpanningFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" merges body cells across rows and columns ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spanRows"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spanColumns"},{"type":"text","value":", with span-aware cell selection), and header groups now compute "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.rowSpan"},{"type":"text","value":" so shallow columns can span header rows. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./cell-spanning.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell Spanning Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refreshed Features"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"More capable features"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Aggregation, Row Selection, Column Pinning, and Column Resizing have all been made more feature rich (multiple aggregation definitions per column, Shift range selection, logical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" pinning, and more)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New core APIs"}]},{"type":"text","value":": New table and row APIs (like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getMaxSubRowDepth()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getDisplayIndex()"},{"type":"text","value":") round out the core feature set."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"7-modern-builds","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7. Modern Builds"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ESM-only"}]},{"type":"text","value":": UMD and CJS builds have been dropped. Packages ship as modern ESM."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript target "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ES2022"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Compiled output now targets ES2022."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Smaller install size"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Published packages no longer ship "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src"},{"type":"text","value":" or source maps, which reduces install footprint."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"the-good-news-most-table-logic-is-still-familiar","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Good News: Most Table Logic Is Still Familiar"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column definitions keep the same basic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessorKey"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessorFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" shapes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature APIs like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.nextPage()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.toggleSorting()"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.toggleSelected()"},{"type":"text","value":" remain the preferred way to update state."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Templates still render header groups, rows, and cells from the table instance."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The main migration is replacing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useVueTable"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTable"},{"type":"text","value":", then moving feature and row-model setup into the v9 shape."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"core-breaking-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core Breaking Changes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hook-rename","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook Rename"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\nimport { useVueTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable(options)\n\n// v9\nimport { useTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useTable(options)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"new-required-features-table-option","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New Required "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" Table Option"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In Table V9, you must explicitly declare which features your table uses. Features, Row Models, and Row Model processing \"Fns\" are defined on the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" table option."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Table V8\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  sortingFns,\n  useVueTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable({\n  columns,\n  data,\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  sortingFns,\n})\n\n// Table V9\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n  useTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\n// All table options that concern including code modules (features, row models, Fns, etc.)\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature, // new - import and pass the feature you want to use\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(), // now row models are defined on the features object\n  sortFns, // now Fns are defined on the features object\n  // ...more features, row models, etc.\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features, // new required option\n  columns,\n  data,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" can be a raw array, a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ref"},{"type":"text","value":", a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computed"},{"type":"text","value":", or a getter. The adapter unwraps reactive option values and keeps the table synced."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"shortcut-use-stockfeatures-for-table-v8-like-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shortcut: Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" for Table V8-like Behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" is useful for early migration before you audit feature usage."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { stockFeatures, useTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features: stockFeatures,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use it as a temporary migration shortcut. Explicit feature registration is the production target."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"available-features","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available Features"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import Name"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Faceting"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnFacetingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Filtering"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnFilteringFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Grouping"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnGroupingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Ordering"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnOrderingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Pinning"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinningFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Resizing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnResizingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Sizing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnSizingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibilityFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global Filtering"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"globalFilteringFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Aggregation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowAggregationFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Expanding"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowExpandingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Pagination"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowPaginationFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Pinning"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowPinningFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Selection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowSelectionFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Sorting"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowSortingFeature"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"row-model-factories","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Model Factories"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row model factories now live on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" object (passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":"). The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowModels"},{"type":"text","value":" option has been removed. Function registries ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":") are also slots on the features object. Row model slots are type-checked, so each row model must be specified after its associated feature in the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"migration-mapping","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration Mapping"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table V8 Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table V9 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" Slot"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table V9 Factory Function"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCoreRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(automatic)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not needed, always included"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFilteredRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filteredRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFilteredRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSortedRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortedRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSortedRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPaginationRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"paginatedRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createPaginatedRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getExpandedRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expandedRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createExpandedRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGroupedRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupedRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGroupedRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facetedRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFacetedRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedMinMaxValues()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facetedMinMaxValues"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFacetedMinMaxValues()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedUniqueValues()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facetedUniqueValues"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFacetedUniqueValues()"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"full-migration-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full Migration Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortingFns,\n  useVueTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable({\n  columns,\n  data,\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortingFns,\n})\n\n// v9\nimport {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n  useTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"prefer-individual-fn-imports-over-full-registries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer Individual Fn Imports Over Full Registries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" registry exports are now deprecated in favor of importing individual "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFn_*"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFn_*"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn_*"},{"type":"text","value":" functions and registering only the ones you use (or passing functions directly in column definitions with no registration at all). The full registries still work, but spreading them puts every built-in function in your bundle. String names, including the default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'auto'"},{"type":"text","value":", only resolve functions you have registered."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Before: registers every built-in function\nimport { filterFns, sortFns } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\n// After: registers only the functions you use\nimport {\n  filterFn_includesString,\n  sortFn_alphanumeric,\n  sortFn_text,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns: { includesString: filterFn_includesString },\n  sortFns: { alphanumeric: sortFn_alphanumeric, text: sortFn_text },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"instance-methods-must-be-called-on-their-instance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instance Methods Must Be Called on Their Instance"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v9, methods on rows, cells, columns, headers, and similar table objects are shared on the object's prototype instead of being created as arrow functions on each object. This improves memory usage, but it means destructuring those methods loses the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":" context they need to operate on the instance."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8 - worked because getValue closed over the row object\nconst { getValue } = row\nconst value = getValue('name')\n\n// v9 - call the method on the instance\nconst value = row.getValue('name')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This applies to row, cell, column, header, and related instance APIs, but not to the table instance itself. Audit code that destructures methods from table objects or passes them around as bare callbacks. Prefer calling them through the original object, for example "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getValue('name')"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.getContext()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getCanSort()"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.getContext()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because these methods now live on the prototype, they also do not appear as own properties in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.keys(instance)"},{"type":"text","value":", object spread, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSON.stringify"},{"type":"text","value":". A shallow clone like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ ...row }"},{"type":"text","value":" copies row data but does not copy row methods. The methods are still callable normally because JavaScript looks them up through the prototype chain."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue v9 table state is atom-backed and Vue-aware. Prefer Vue "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computed"},{"type":"text","value":" values around narrow atom reads over broad whole-state reads."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Surface"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.atoms.<slice>.get()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Narrow reactive reads inside Vue tracking scopes."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.store.get()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current full state snapshot. Use mostly for debug output or intentionally broad dependencies."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.Subscribe"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated compatibility wrapper. Read table APIs or atoms in native Vue reactive contexts."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.baseAtoms.<slice>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Internal writable atoms. Prefer feature APIs or external atoms."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"accessing-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accessing State"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\nconst sorting = table.getState().sorting\n\n// v9: narrow atom read\nconst sorting = table.atoms.sorting.get()\n\n// v9: full snapshot\nconst tableState = table.store.get()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Vue primitives to derive reactive values:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { computed } from 'vue'\n\nconst pagination = computed(() => table.atoms.pagination.get())\nconst pageIndex = computed(() => pagination.value.pageIndex)\nconst tableStateJson = computed(() =>\n  JSON.stringify(table.store.get(), null, 2),\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reactive-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" can be a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ref"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computed"},{"type":"text","value":"; the adapter unwraps and syncs it."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ref } from 'vue'\n\nconst data = ref(makeData(100))\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n\ndata.value = makeData(200)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getter-based options also work:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data.value\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"replace-table-subscribe","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.Subscribe"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" is deprecated. It only passes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.atoms"},{"type":"text","value":" to its child function and adds no subscription logic. Read table APIs or atoms directly inside templates, render functions, computed values, or watcher sources."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, return this JSX from a component's render function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<span>Page {table.atoms.pagination.get().pageIndex + 1}</span>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you used "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" as a component to isolate rendering, move those reads into a child component. Calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" as a plain function never created a separate component render boundary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"controlled-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Controlled State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v8-style "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"on[State]Change"},{"type":"text","value":" controlled state patterns still work and remain convenient for simple integrations. For new v9 code, prefer owning state slices with external atoms (see "},{"type":"link","href":"#external-atoms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"External Atoms"}]},{"type":"text","value":" below), which give you fine-grained subscriptions without mirroring state through Vue refs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When Vue refs own a state slice, expose the current value with getters and update the ref in the matching callback."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ref } from 'vue'\nimport type {\n  PaginationState,\n  SortingState,\n  Updater,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nfunction resolveUpdater<T>(updater: Updater<T>, previous: T): T {\n  return typeof updater === 'function'\n    ? (updater as (old: T) => T)(previous)\n    : updater\n}\n\nconst sorting = ref<SortingState>([])\nconst pagination = ref<PaginationState>({\n  pageIndex: 0,\n  pageSize: 10,\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data.value\n  },\n  state: {\n    get sorting() {\n      return sorting.value\n    },\n    get pagination() {\n      return pagination.value\n    },\n  },\n  onSortingChange: (updater) => {\n    sorting.value = resolveUpdater(updater, sorting.value)\n  },\n  onPaginationChange: (updater) => {\n    pagination.value = resolveUpdater(updater, pagination.value)\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v8-style top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStateChange"},{"type":"text","value":" callback is gone. Use per-slice callbacks or external atoms."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want to lift or listen to any state change, set up a subscription to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.store"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const unsubscribe = table.store.subscribe((state) => {\n  console.log(state)\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"external-atoms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"External Atoms"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use external atoms when the app should own and share state slices outside the table."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createAtom, useSelector } from '@tanstack/vue-store'\nimport type { PaginationState, SortingState } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst sortingAtom = createAtom<SortingState>([])\nconst paginationAtom = createAtom<PaginationState>({\n  pageIndex: 0,\n  pageSize: 10,\n})\n\nconst pagination = useSelector(paginationAtom)\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data.value\n  },\n  atoms: {\n    sorting: sortingAtom,\n    pagination: paginationAtom,\n  },\n})\n\npagination.value.pageIndex","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not provide both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"atoms.pagination"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.pagination"},{"type":"text","value":"; the atom owns that slice."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"feature-by-feature-breaking-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature-by-Feature Breaking Changes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sorting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorting"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v9"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFn"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFn"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFns"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSortingFn()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSortFn()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAutoSortingFn()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAutoSortFn()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortingFn"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortFn"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"column-pinning","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Pinning"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"V9 changes column pinning to use logical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" terminology instead of the physical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"left"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"right"},{"type":"text","value":" terminology used in V8. In LTR languages/layouts, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" usually corresponds to left and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" to right; in RTL languages/layouts, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" usually corresponds to right and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" to left. There are no deprecated aliases."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"V8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"V9"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinning.left"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinning.start"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinning.right"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinning.end"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.pin('left')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.pin('start')"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.pin('right')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.pin('end')"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsPinned() === 'left'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsPinned() === 'start'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsPinned() === 'right'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsPinned() === 'end'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getLeftVisibleCells()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getStartVisibleCells()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getRightVisibleCells()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getEndVisibleCells()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getLeftHeaderGroups()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getStartHeaderGroups()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getRightHeaderGroups()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getEndHeaderGroups()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getLeftLeafColumns()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getStartLeafColumns()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getRightLeafColumns()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getEndLeafColumns()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getLeftVisibleLeafColumns()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getStartVisibleLeafColumns()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getRightVisibleLeafColumns()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getEndVisibleLeafColumns()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getLeftTotalSize()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getStartTotalSize()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getRightTotalSize()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getEndTotalSize()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getStart('left')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getStart('start')"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAfter('right')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAfter('end')"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIndex('left')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIndex('start')"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIndex('right')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIndex('end')"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This rename is about logical table regions, not automatic DOM direction handling. For sticky column pinning, prefer CSS logical properties like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"insetInlineStart"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"insetInlineEnd"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnResizeDirection"},{"type":"text","value":" table option is unchanged."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The table-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enablePinning"},{"type":"text","value":" option has also been split into separate options:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableColumnPinning: true\nenableRowPinning: true","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"column-sizing-vs-column-resizing-split","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Sizing vs. Column Resizing Split"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column resizing now has its own feature and state slice."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({\n  columnSizingFeature,\n  columnResizingFeature,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnSizingInfo"},{"type":"text","value":" became "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnResizing"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setColumnSizingInfo()"},{"type":"text","value":" became "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setColumnResizing()"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onColumnSizingInfoChange"},{"type":"text","value":" became "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onColumnResizingChange"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"grouping-and-aggregation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouping and Aggregation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aggregation is now its own feature, independent from column grouping. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" still includes both, so tables using it need no feature-registration change. If you declare features explicitly, add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowAggregationFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" whenever columns use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAggregationValue"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.getIsAggregated"},{"type":"text","value":". Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnGroupingFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupedRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":" only when you also group rows."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature, // only for grouped rows\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  aggregationFns: { sum: aggregationFn_sum },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom aggregation callables have changed to context-based definitions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\nconst total = (columnId, leafRows, childRows) =>\n  leafRows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + row.getValue(columnId), 0)\n\n// Current V9\nconst total = constructAggregationFn({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + Number(getValue(row)), 0),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The old per-function choice between "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"childRows"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"leafRows"},{"type":"text","value":" is replaced by a single depth-selected "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context.rows"},{"type":"text","value":", controlled by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxAggregationDepth"},{"type":"text","value":" column option. The default ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":") preserves V8's direct-child grouped aggregation; use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Infinity"},{"type":"text","value":" to aggregate terminal leaf rows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAggregationValue()"},{"type":"text","value":" now takes a single options object instead of positional arguments:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\ncolumn.getAggregationValue(rows, maxDepth)\n\n// Current V9\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows, maxDepth })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAggregationFn()"},{"type":"text","value":" is now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAggregationFns()"},{"type":"text","value":" because a column can run multiple definitions, and the old callable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CreatedAggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":" types are replaced by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AggregationFnDef"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./grouping","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouping Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and the "},{"type":"link","href":"./aggregation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aggregation Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for full documentation of the new capabilities."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"row-selection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Selection"}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"warning","title":"Warning","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Minor breaking change:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getToggleSelectedHandler()"},{"type":"text","value":" now enables inclusive Shift range selection by default when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowSelectionFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" is enabled. Existing checkboxes or rows wired through this handler establish an anchor on an ordinary interaction and select or deselect the current display-order range on a Shift interaction. Direct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.toggleSelected()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls are unchanged."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableRowRangeSelection: false"},{"type":"text","value":" to preserve the previous non-range handler behavior. The handler must receive an event that exposes Shift directly or through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nativeEvent"},{"type":"text","value":"; see "},{"type":"link","href":"./row-selection.md#shift-range-selection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shift Range Selection"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The \"some rows selected\" checks were simplified to mean \"at least one row is selected\":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v9"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getIsSomeRowsSelected()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when some but not all rows are selected"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when at least one row is selected"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getIsSomePageRowsSelected()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when some but not all page rows are selected"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when at least one page row is selected"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v8 these returned "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" once every row was selected; in v9 they stay "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":". If you use them to drive an indeterminate \"select all\" checkbox, gate the indeterminate state on the matching all-selected check so it clears at full selection:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsSomeRowsSelected() && !getIsAllRowsSelected()"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"row-and-internal-api-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row and Internal API Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some row APIs have changed from private to public:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table V8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table V9"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row._getAllCellsByColumnId()"},{"type":"text","value":" (private)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getAllCellsByColumnId()"},{"type":"text","value":" (public)"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All other internal APIs prefixed with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_"},{"type":"text","value":" have been removed. If you were using any of these, use their public equivalents:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removed: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table._getPinnedRows()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removed: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table._getFacetedRowModel()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removed: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table._getFacetedMinMaxValues()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removed: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table._getFacetedUniqueValues()"}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-helper-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Helper Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column helpers and column types now include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" first."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<Person>()\nconst columns: ColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    sortingFn: 'alphanumeric',\n  }),\n]\n\n// v9\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\nconst columns: Array<ColumnDef<typeof features, Person>> = columnHelper.columns(\n  [\n    columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n      header: 'Age',\n      sortFn: 'alphanumeric',\n    }),\n  ],\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnHelper.columns([...])"},{"type":"text","value":" for better inference across nested columns."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rendering-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v9 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" component supports shorthand props for cells, headers, and footers."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- v8 -->\n<FlexRender :render=\"cell.column.columnDef.cell\" :props=\"cell.getContext()\" />\n\n<!-- v9 preferred -->\n<FlexRender :cell=\"cell\" />\n<FlexRender :header=\"header\" />\n<FlexRender :footer=\"footer\" />","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The older "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":render"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":props"},{"type":"text","value":" shape still compiles, but the shorthand props are the preferred migration target."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-tableoptions-utility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions()"},{"type":"text","value":" Utility"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions()"},{"type":"text","value":" helps compose shared table option fragments."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { tableOptions } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst baseOptions = tableOptions({\n  features,\n  defaultColumn: {\n    minSize: 40,\n  },\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  ...baseOptions,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createtablehook-composable-table-patterns","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":": Composable Table Patterns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" creates shared Vue table helpers with features, row models, and registered components already bound."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createTableHook } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst { useAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n})\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst table = useAppTable({\n  columns,\n  data,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./composable-tables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composable Tables Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for full patterns."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typescript-changes-summary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript Changes Summary"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"type-generics","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Generics"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" as the first generic:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"ColumnDef<typeof features, Person>\nColumn<typeof features, Person>\nRow<typeof features, Person>\nTable<typeof features, Person>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-typeof-features","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof features"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n})\n\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-stockfeatures","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StockFeatures"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { StockFeatures } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\ntype PersonColumn = ColumnDef<StockFeatures, Person>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tablemeta-columnmeta-typing-changes","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ColumnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" Typing Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No more declaration merging required! (Although it still works if you want to keep using it)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global declaration merging works exactly like it did in v8. The only change you need to make is updating the generics shape: both interfaces now take "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" as the first type parameter."}]},{"type":"code","value":"declare module '@tanstack/vue-table' {\n  interface ColumnMeta<TFeatures, TData, TValue> {\n    align?: 'left' | 'right'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That's all that's required if you want to keep declaring meta types globally."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optionally, v9 also adds a new way to declare meta types "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per-table"}]},{"type":"text","value":" without declaration merging. You can use type-only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" slots on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" option, which only affect tables created with that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" object:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<{ align?: 'left' | 'right' }>(),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the new "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../guide/table-and-column-meta","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table and Column Meta Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for full details on both approaches."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"filterfns-sortfns-aggregationfns-filtermeta-augmentation-replaced-by-registry-slots","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterFns"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortFns"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" Augmentation Replaced by Registry Slots"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v8, making a custom function usable as a string reference (like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFn: 'fuzzy'"},{"type":"text","value":") required "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"declare module"},{"type":"text","value":" augmentation of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterFns"},{"type":"text","value":" interface, and typing filter meta required augmenting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":". In v9, registering the function in the matching registry slot does both jobs with no global augmentation:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\ndeclare module '@tanstack/vue-table' {\n  interface FilterFns {\n    fuzzy: FilterFn<unknown>\n  }\n  interface FilterMeta {\n    itemRank: RankingInfo\n  }\n}\n\n// v9 - register in the slot; the key becomes a valid string value\ninterface FuzzyFilterMeta {\n  itemRank?: RankingInfo\n}\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  filterFns: { fuzzy: fuzzyFilter },\n  filterMeta: metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>(),\n})\n\n// 'fuzzy' now typechecks in column defs for tables using these features\ncolumnHelper.accessor('name', { filterFn: 'fuzzy' })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same pattern applies to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":" (for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFn"},{"type":"text","value":" string values) and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" (for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":" string values). See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./fuzzy-filtering.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fuzzy Filtering Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for a complete example."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rowdata-type-restriction","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RowData"},{"type":"text","value":" Type Restriction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer explicit object row types:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"migration-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration Checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useVueTable"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTable"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures()"},{"type":"text","value":" (or use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move row model factories into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" as slots (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel()"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remove "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCoreRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":"; the core row model is automatic."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" as slots (row model factories no longer take arguments)."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace destructured row/cell/column/header methods with calls on the instance (for example, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getValue('name')"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getState()"},{"type":"text","value":" reads with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.atoms.<slice>.get()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.store.get()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Vue getters for controlled "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" slices."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStateChange"},{"type":"text","value":" with per-slice callbacks or external atoms."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rename "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFn"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFn"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convert custom aggregation callables to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"constructAggregationFn({ aggregate, merge? })"},{"type":"text","value":" definitions."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof features"},{"type":"text","value":" to column helpers and types."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"declare module"},{"type":"text","value":" augmentation of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterFns"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortFns"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" with registry-slot registration, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" augmentation with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" slot."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<FlexRender :cell=\"cell\" />"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":header"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":footer"},{"type":"text","value":" shorthand rendering."}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" before production."}]}],"checked":false}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic-use-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic useTable"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic-external-atoms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic External Atoms"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic-external-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic External State"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/with-tanstack-query","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With TanStack Query"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/sorting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorting"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/pagination","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pagination"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/composable-tables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composable Tables"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"what-s-new-in-tanstack-table-v9","text":"What's New in TanStack Table V9","level":2},{"id":"1-better-performance","text":"1. Better Performance","level":3},{"id":"2-state-management-overhaul","text":"2. State Management Overhaul","level":3},{"id":"3-type-safety-improvements","text":"3. Type-Safety Improvements","level":3},{"id":"4-tree-shaking-and-extensibility","text":"4. Tree Shaking and Extensibility","level":3},{"id":"5-composability","text":"5. Composability","level":3},{"id":"6-new-and-refreshed-features","text":"6. New and Refreshed Features","level":3},{"id":"7-modern-builds","text":"7. Modern Builds","level":3},{"id":"the-good-news-most-table-logic-is-still-familiar","text":"The Good News: Most Table Logic Is Still Familiar","level":3},{"id":"core-breaking-changes","text":"Core Breaking Changes","level":2},{"id":"hook-rename","text":"Hook Rename","level":3},{"id":"new-required-features-table-option","text":"New Required features Table Option","level":3},{"id":"shortcut-use-stockfeatures-for-table-v8-like-behavior","text":"Shortcut: Use stockFeatures for Table V8-like Behavior","level":4},{"id":"available-features","text":"Available Features","level":3},{"id":"row-model-factories","text":"Row Model Factories","level":3},{"id":"migration-mapping","text":"Migration Mapping","level":4},{"id":"full-migration-example","text":"Full Migration Example","level":4},{"id":"prefer-individual-fn-imports-over-full-registries","text":"Prefer Individual Fn Imports Over Full Registries","level":4},{"id":"instance-methods-must-be-called-on-their-instance","text":"Instance Methods Must Be Called on Their Instance","level":3},{"id":"state-management-changes","text":"State Management Changes","level":2},{"id":"accessing-state","text":"Accessing State","level":3},{"id":"reactive-options","text":"Reactive Options","level":3},{"id":"replace-table-subscribe","text":"Replace table.Subscribe","level":3},{"id":"controlled-state","text":"Controlled State","level":3},{"id":"external-atoms","text":"External Atoms","level":3},{"id":"feature-by-feature-breaking-changes","text":"Feature-by-Feature Breaking Changes","level":2},{"id":"sorting","text":"Sorting","level":3},{"id":"column-pinning","text":"Column Pinning","level":3},{"id":"column-sizing-vs-column-resizing-split","text":"Column Sizing vs. Column Resizing Split","level":3},{"id":"grouping-and-aggregation","text":"Grouping and Aggregation","level":3},{"id":"row-selection","text":"Row Selection","level":3},{"id":"row-and-internal-api-changes","text":"Row and Internal API Changes","level":3},{"id":"column-helper-changes","text":"Column Helper Changes","level":2},{"id":"rendering-changes","text":"Rendering Changes","level":2},{"id":"the-tableoptions-utility","text":"The tableOptions() Utility","level":2},{"id":"createtablehook-composable-table-patterns","text":"createTableHook: Composable Table Patterns","level":2},{"id":"typescript-changes-summary","text":"TypeScript Changes Summary","level":2},{"id":"type-generics","text":"Type Generics","level":3},{"id":"using-typeof-features","text":"Using typeof features","level":3},{"id":"using-stockfeatures","text":"Using StockFeatures","level":3},{"id":"tablemeta-columnmeta-typing-changes","text":"TableMeta/ColumnMeta Typing Changes","level":3},{"id":"filterfns-sortfns-aggregationfns-filtermeta-augmentation-replaced-by-registry-slots","text":"FilterFns/SortFns/AggregationFns/FilterMeta Augmentation Replaced by Registry Slots","level":3},{"id":"rowdata-type-restriction","text":"RowData Type Restriction","level":3},{"id":"migration-checklist","text":"Migration Checklist","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## What's New in TanStack Table V9\n\nTanStack Table V9 delivers major performance improvements, hundreds of bug fixes, new and refreshed features, and optional helpers for composing and managing tables. Despite the scale of the release, the headless model, core table logic, column definitions, and rendering patterns remain familiar. Here are the key changes:\n\n### 1. Better Performance\n\n- **Lower memory usage**: The core architecture now shares more behavior across table objects, with some large-table scenarios seeing up to 90% memory savings.\n- **Faster client-side row models**: Sorting, filtering, and aggregation paths have improved algorithms and memoization, with many scenarios seeing up to 40-70% speed improvements.\n- **Better column resizing performance**: The same architectural and memoization work also speeds up column resizing.\n\n### 2. State Management Overhaul\n\n- **TanStack Store foundation**: Table state is backed by TanStack Store atoms.\n- **Vue reactivity integration**: Table atoms are backed by Vue refs and computed values, and `useTable` unwraps reactive option values like `data`.\n- **Fine-grained subscriptions**: Registered features expose per-slice state through `table.atoms`, so reads can stay scoped to the state they need.\n\n### 3. Type-Safety Improvements\n\n- **New and revamped type helpers**: There are helpers for defining columns, custom filters, sorts, aggregations, column and table meta, shared table options and components, and more.\n- **Per-table meta types**: `tableMeta`, `columnMeta`, and `filterMeta` slots let you type meta for a specific table instead of globally augmenting shared interfaces. **No more global declaration merging required!**\n- **Feature-gated APIs**: APIs only exist when their feature is registered, and `tableFeatures()` validates feature prerequisites at the type level.\n\n### 4. Tree Shaking and Extensibility\n\n- **Import only the features you use**: Tables that only need sorting do not ship filtering, pagination, or other unused feature code.\n- **Tree-shakeable row models and functions**: Row model factories and `filterFns` / `sortFns` / `aggregationFns` now live on `tableFeatures()`, so unused processing code can be dropped.\n- **Custom features use the same system**: Your own feature plugins can register state, options, and APIs alongside the built-in features. See the [Custom Features Guide](./custom-features.md).\n\n### 5. Composability\n\n- **`tableOptions()`**: Compose reusable table configuration, including features, row models, and default options.\n- **`createTableHook()`**: Define shared Vue table factories with pre-bound features, row models, defaults, and components.\n\n### 6. New and Refreshed Features\n\n- **New Features**\n  - **Cell Selection**: `cellSelectionFeature` adds spreadsheet-style rectangular cell range selection, with drag, Shift-extend, and multiple disjoint ranges. See the [Cell Selection Guide](./cell-selection.md).\n  - **Cell Spanning**: `cellSpanningFeature` merges body cells across rows and columns (`spanRows` / `spanColumns`, with span-aware cell selection), and header groups now compute `header.rowSpan` so shallow columns can span header rows. See the [Cell Spanning Guide](./cell-spanning.md).\n- **Refreshed Features**\n  - **More capable features**: Aggregation, Row Selection, Column Pinning, and Column Resizing have all been made more feature rich (multiple aggregation definitions per column, Shift range selection, logical `start`/`end` pinning, and more).\n  - **New core APIs**: New table and row APIs (like `table.getMaxSubRowDepth()`, `row.getDisplayIndex()`) round out the core feature set.\n\n### 7. Modern Builds\n\n- **ESM-only**: UMD and CJS builds have been dropped. Packages ship as modern ESM.\n- **TypeScript target `ES2022`**: Compiled output now targets ES2022.\n- **Smaller install size**: Published packages no longer ship `src` or source maps, which reduces install footprint.\n\n### The Good News: Most Table Logic Is Still Familiar\n\n- Column definitions keep the same basic `accessorKey`, `accessorFn`, `header`, `cell`, and `footer` shapes.\n- Feature APIs like `table.nextPage()`, `column.toggleSorting()`, and `row.toggleSelected()` remain the preferred way to update state.\n- Templates still render header groups, rows, and cells from the table instance.\n\nThe main migration is replacing `useVueTable` with `useTable`, then moving feature and row-model setup into the v9 shape.\n\n---\n\n## Core Breaking Changes\n\n### Hook Rename\n\n```ts\n// v8\nimport { useVueTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable(options)\n\n// v9\nimport { useTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useTable(options)\n```\n\n### New Required `features` Table Option\n\nIn Table V9, you must explicitly declare which features your table uses. Features, Row Models, and Row Model processing \"Fns\" are defined on the new `features` table option.\n\n```ts\n// Table V8\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  sortingFns,\n  useVueTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable({\n  columns,\n  data,\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  sortingFns,\n})\n\n// Table V9\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n  useTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\n// All table options that concern including code modules (features, row models, Fns, etc.)\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature, // new - import and pass the feature you want to use\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(), // now row models are defined on the features object\n  sortFns, // now Fns are defined on the features object\n  // ...more features, row models, etc.\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features, // new required option\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\n`data` can be a raw array, a `ref`, a `computed`, or a getter. The adapter unwraps reactive option values and keeps the table synced.\n\n#### Shortcut: Use `stockFeatures` for Table V8-like Behavior\n\n`stockFeatures` is useful for early migration before you audit feature usage.\n\n```ts\nimport { stockFeatures, useTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features: stockFeatures,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\nUse it as a temporary migration shortcut. Explicit feature registration is the production target.\n\n### Available Features\n\n| Feature           | Import Name               |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Column Faceting   | `columnFacetingFeature`   |\n| Column Filtering  | `columnFilteringFeature`  |\n| Column Grouping   | `columnGroupingFeature`   |\n| Column Ordering   | `columnOrderingFeature`   |\n| Column Pinning    | `columnPinningFeature`    |\n| Column Resizing   | `columnResizingFeature`   |\n| Column Sizing     | `columnSizingFeature`     |\n| Column Visibility | `columnVisibilityFeature` |\n| Global Filtering  | `globalFilteringFeature`  |\n| Row Aggregation   | `rowAggregationFeature`   |\n| Row Expanding     | `rowExpandingFeature`     |\n| Row Pagination    | `rowPaginationFeature`    |\n| Row Pinning       | `rowPinningFeature`       |\n| Row Selection     | `rowSelectionFeature`     |\n| Row Sorting       | `rowSortingFeature`       |\n\n### Row Model Factories\n\nRow model factories now live on the `features` object (passed to `tableFeatures`). The `rowModels` option has been removed. Function registries (`filterFns`, `sortFns`, `aggregationFns`) are also slots on the features object. Row model slots are type-checked, so each row model must be specified after its associated feature in the same `tableFeatures` call.\n\n#### Migration Mapping\n\n| Table V8 Option            | Table V9 `tableFeatures` Slot | Table V9 Factory Function     |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `getCoreRowModel()`        | (automatic)                   | Not needed, always included   |\n| `getFilteredRowModel()`    | `filteredRowModel`            | `createFilteredRowModel()`    |\n| `getSortedRowModel()`      | `sortedRowModel`              | `createSortedRowModel()`      |\n| `getPaginationRowModel()`  | `paginatedRowModel`           | `createPaginatedRowModel()`   |\n| `getExpandedRowModel()`    | `expandedRowModel`            | `createExpandedRowModel()`    |\n| `getGroupedRowModel()`     | `groupedRowModel`             | `createGroupedRowModel()`     |\n| `getFacetedRowModel()`     | `facetedRowModel`             | `createFacetedRowModel()`     |\n| `getFacetedMinMaxValues()` | `facetedMinMaxValues`         | `createFacetedMinMaxValues()` |\n| `getFacetedUniqueValues()` | `facetedUniqueValues`         | `createFacetedUniqueValues()` |\n\n#### Full Migration Example\n\n```ts\n// v8\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortingFns,\n  useVueTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable({\n  columns,\n  data,\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortingFns,\n})\n\n// v9\nimport {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n  useTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\n#### Prefer Individual Fn Imports Over Full Registries\n\nThe `filterFns`, `sortFns`, and `aggregationFns` registry exports are now deprecated in favor of importing individual `filterFn_*`, `sortFn_*`, and `aggregationFn_*` functions and registering only the ones you use (or passing functions directly in column definitions with no registration at all). The full registries still work, but spreading them puts every built-in function in your bundle. String names, including the default `'auto'`, only resolve functions you have registered.\n\n```ts\n// Before: registers every built-in function\nimport { filterFns, sortFns } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\n// After: registers only the functions you use\nimport {\n  filterFn_includesString,\n  sortFn_alphanumeric,\n  sortFn_text,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns: { includesString: filterFn_includesString },\n  sortFns: { alphanumeric: sortFn_alphanumeric, text: sortFn_text },\n})\n```\n\n### Instance Methods Must Be Called on Their Instance\n\nIn v9, methods on rows, cells, columns, headers, and similar table objects are shared on the object's prototype instead of being created as arrow functions on each object. This improves memory usage, but it means destructuring those methods loses the `this` context they need to operate on the instance.\n\n```ts\n// v8 - worked because getValue closed over the row object\nconst { getValue } = row\nconst value = getValue('name')\n\n// v9 - call the method on the instance\nconst value = row.getValue('name')\n```\n\nThis applies to row, cell, column, header, and related instance APIs, but not to the table instance itself. Audit code that destructures methods from table objects or passes them around as bare callbacks. Prefer calling them through the original object, for example `row.getValue('name')`, `cell.getContext()`, `column.getCanSort()`, or `header.getContext()`.\n\nBecause these methods now live on the prototype, they also do not appear as own properties in `Object.keys(instance)`, object spread, or `JSON.stringify`. A shallow clone like `{ ...row }` copies row data but does not copy row methods. The methods are still callable normally because JavaScript looks them up through the prototype chain.\n\n---\n\n## State Management Changes\n\nVue v9 table state is atom-backed and Vue-aware. Prefer Vue `computed` values around narrow atom reads over broad whole-state reads.\n\n| Surface                     | Use                                                                                           |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `table.atoms.<slice>.get()` | Narrow reactive reads inside Vue tracking scopes.                                             |\n| `table.store.get()`         | Current full state snapshot. Use mostly for debug output or intentionally broad dependencies. |\n| `table.Subscribe`           | Deprecated compatibility wrapper. Read table APIs or atoms in native Vue reactive contexts.   |\n| `table.baseAtoms.<slice>`   | Internal writable atoms. Prefer feature APIs or external atoms.                               |\n\n### Accessing State\n\n```ts\n// v8\nconst sorting = table.getState().sorting\n\n// v9: narrow atom read\nconst sorting = table.atoms.sorting.get()\n\n// v9: full snapshot\nconst tableState = table.store.get()\n```\n\nUse Vue primitives to derive reactive values:\n\n```ts\nimport { computed } from 'vue'\n\nconst pagination = computed(() => table.atoms.pagination.get())\nconst pageIndex = computed(() => pagination.value.pageIndex)\nconst tableStateJson = computed(() =>\n  JSON.stringify(table.store.get(), null, 2),\n)\n```\n\n### Reactive Options\n\n`data` can be a `ref` or `computed`; the adapter unwraps and syncs it.\n\n```ts\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\n\nconst data = ref(makeData(100))\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n\ndata.value = makeData(200)\n```\n\nGetter-based options also work:\n\n```ts\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data.value\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Replace `table.Subscribe`\n\n`table.Subscribe` is deprecated. It only passes `table.atoms` to its child function and adds no subscription logic. Read table APIs or atoms directly inside templates, render functions, computed values, or watcher sources.\n\nFor example, return this JSX from a component's render function:\n\n```tsx\n<span>Page {table.atoms.pagination.get().pageIndex + 1}</span>\n```\n\nIf you used `table.Subscribe` as a component to isolate rendering, move those reads into a child component. Calling `table.Subscribe` as a plain function never created a separate component render boundary.\n\n### Controlled State\n\nThe v8-style `state` + `on[State]Change` controlled state patterns still work and remain convenient for simple integrations. For new v9 code, prefer owning state slices with external atoms (see [External Atoms](#external-atoms) below), which give you fine-grained subscriptions without mirroring state through Vue refs.\n\nWhen Vue refs own a state slice, expose the current value with getters and update the ref in the matching callback.\n\n```ts\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport type {\n  PaginationState,\n  SortingState,\n  Updater,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nfunction resolveUpdater<T>(updater: Updater<T>, previous: T): T {\n  return typeof updater === 'function'\n    ? (updater as (old: T) => T)(previous)\n    : updater\n}\n\nconst sorting = ref<SortingState>([])\nconst pagination = ref<PaginationState>({\n  pageIndex: 0,\n  pageSize: 10,\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data.value\n  },\n  state: {\n    get sorting() {\n      return sorting.value\n    },\n    get pagination() {\n      return pagination.value\n    },\n  },\n  onSortingChange: (updater) => {\n    sorting.value = resolveUpdater(updater, sorting.value)\n  },\n  onPaginationChange: (updater) => {\n    pagination.value = resolveUpdater(updater, pagination.value)\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe v8-style top-level `onStateChange` callback is gone. Use per-slice callbacks or external atoms.\n\nIf you want to lift or listen to any state change, set up a subscription to the `table.store`:\n\n```ts\nconst unsubscribe = table.store.subscribe((state) => {\n  console.log(state)\n})\n```\n\n### External Atoms\n\nUse external atoms when the app should own and share state slices outside the table.\n\n```ts\nimport { createAtom, useSelector } from '@tanstack/vue-store'\nimport type { PaginationState, SortingState } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst sortingAtom = createAtom<SortingState>([])\nconst paginationAtom = createAtom<PaginationState>({\n  pageIndex: 0,\n  pageSize: 10,\n})\n\nconst pagination = useSelector(paginationAtom)\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data.value\n  },\n  atoms: {\n    sorting: sortingAtom,\n    pagination: paginationAtom,\n  },\n})\n\npagination.value.pageIndex\n```\n\nDo not provide both `atoms.pagination` and `state.pagination`; the atom owns that slice.\n\n---\n\n## Feature-by-Feature Breaking Changes\n\n### Sorting\n\n| v8                   | v9                |\n| -------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `sortingFn`          | `sortFn`          |\n| `sortingFns`         | `sortFns`         |\n| `getSortingFn()`     | `getSortFn()`     |\n| `getAutoSortingFn()` | `getAutoSortFn()` |\n| `SortingFn`          | `SortFn`          |\n\n### Column Pinning\n\nV9 changes column pinning to use logical `start`/`end` terminology instead of the physical `left`/`right` terminology used in V8. In LTR languages/layouts, `start` usually corresponds to left and `end` to right; in RTL languages/layouts, `start` usually corresponds to right and `end` to left. There are no deprecated aliases.\n\n| V8                                   | V9                                   |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `columnPinning.left`                 | `columnPinning.start`                |\n| `columnPinning.right`                | `columnPinning.end`                  |\n| `column.pin('left')`                 | `column.pin('start')`                |\n| `column.pin('right')`                | `column.pin('end')`                  |\n| `column.getIsPinned() === 'left'`    | `column.getIsPinned() === 'start'`   |\n| `column.getIsPinned() === 'right'`   | `column.getIsPinned() === 'end'`     |\n| `row.getLeftVisibleCells()`          | `row.getStartVisibleCells()`         |\n| `row.getRightVisibleCells()`         | `row.getEndVisibleCells()`           |\n| `table.getLeftHeaderGroups()`        | `table.getStartHeaderGroups()`       |\n| `table.getRightHeaderGroups()`       | `table.getEndHeaderGroups()`         |\n| `table.getLeftLeafColumns()`         | `table.getStartLeafColumns()`        |\n| `table.getRightLeafColumns()`        | `table.getEndLeafColumns()`          |\n| `table.getLeftVisibleLeafColumns()`  | `table.getStartVisibleLeafColumns()` |\n| `table.getRightVisibleLeafColumns()` | `table.getEndVisibleLeafColumns()`   |\n| `table.getLeftTotalSize()`           | `table.getStartTotalSize()`          |\n| `table.getRightTotalSize()`          | `table.getEndTotalSize()`            |\n| `column.getStart('left')`            | `column.getStart('start')`           |\n| `column.getAfter('right')`           | `column.getAfter('end')`             |\n| `column.getIndex('left')`            | `column.getIndex('start')`           |\n| `column.getIndex('right')`           | `column.getIndex('end')`             |\n\nThis rename is about logical table regions, not automatic DOM direction handling. For sticky column pinning, prefer CSS logical properties like `insetInlineStart` and `insetInlineEnd`. The `columnResizeDirection` table option is unchanged.\n\nThe table-level `enablePinning` option has also been split into separate options:\n\n```ts\nenableColumnPinning: true\nenableRowPinning: true\n```\n\n### Column Sizing vs. Column Resizing Split\n\nColumn resizing now has its own feature and state slice.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnSizingFeature,\n  columnResizingFeature,\n})\n```\n\n`columnSizingInfo` became `columnResizing`, `setColumnSizingInfo()` became `setColumnResizing()`, and `onColumnSizingInfoChange` became `onColumnResizingChange`.\n\n### Grouping and Aggregation\n\nAggregation is now its own feature, independent from column grouping. `stockFeatures` still includes both, so tables using it need no feature-registration change. If you declare features explicitly, add `rowAggregationFeature` whenever columns use `aggregationFn`, `aggregatedCell`, `getAggregationValue`, or `cell.getIsAggregated`. Add `columnGroupingFeature` and `groupedRowModel` only when you also group rows.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature, // only for grouped rows\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  aggregationFns: { sum: aggregationFn_sum },\n})\n```\n\nCustom aggregation callables have changed to context-based definitions:\n\n```ts\n// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\nconst total = (columnId, leafRows, childRows) =>\n  leafRows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + row.getValue(columnId), 0)\n\n// Current V9\nconst total = constructAggregationFn({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + Number(getValue(row)), 0),\n})\n```\n\nThe old per-function choice between `childRows` and `leafRows` is replaced by a single depth-selected `context.rows`, controlled by the `maxAggregationDepth` column option. The default (`0`) preserves V8's direct-child grouped aggregation; use `Infinity` to aggregate terminal leaf rows.\n\n`column.getAggregationValue()` now takes a single options object instead of positional arguments:\n\n```ts\n// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\ncolumn.getAggregationValue(rows, maxDepth)\n\n// Current V9\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows, maxDepth })\n```\n\n`column.getAggregationFn()` is now `column.getAggregationFns()` because a column can run multiple definitions, and the old callable `AggregationFn`/`CreatedAggregationFn` types are replaced by `AggregationFnDef`.\n\nSee the [Grouping Guide](./grouping) and the [Aggregation Guide](./aggregation) for full documentation of the new capabilities.\n\n### Row Selection\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Minor breaking change:** `row.getToggleSelectedHandler()` now enables inclusive Shift range selection by default when `rowSelectionFeature` is enabled. Existing checkboxes or rows wired through this handler establish an anchor on an ordinary interaction and select or deselect the current display-order range on a Shift interaction. Direct `row.toggleSelected()` calls are unchanged.\n>\n> Set `enableRowRangeSelection: false` to preserve the previous non-range handler behavior. The handler must receive an event that exposes Shift directly or through `nativeEvent`; see [Shift Range Selection](./row-selection.md#shift-range-selection).\n\nThe \"some rows selected\" checks were simplified to mean \"at least one row is selected\":\n\n| API                                 | v8                                                  | v9                                            |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `table.getIsSomeRowsSelected()`     | `true` when some but not all rows are selected      | `true` when at least one row is selected      |\n| `table.getIsSomePageRowsSelected()` | `true` when some but not all page rows are selected | `true` when at least one page row is selected |\n\nIn v8 these returned `false` once every row was selected; in v9 they stay `true`. If you use them to drive an indeterminate \"select all\" checkbox, gate the indeterminate state on the matching all-selected check so it clears at full selection:\n\n`getIsSomeRowsSelected() && !getIsAllRowsSelected()`\n\n### Row and Internal API Changes\n\nSome row APIs have changed from private to public:\n\n| Table V8                                 | Table V9                               |\n| ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `row._getAllCellsByColumnId()` (private) | `row.getAllCellsByColumnId()` (public) |\n\nAll other internal APIs prefixed with `_` have been removed. If you were using any of these, use their public equivalents:\n\n- Removed: `table._getPinnedRows()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedRowModel()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedMinMaxValues()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedUniqueValues()`\n\n---\n\n## Column Helper Changes\n\nColumn helpers and column types now include `TFeatures` first.\n\n```ts\n// v8\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<Person>()\nconst columns: ColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    sortingFn: 'alphanumeric',\n  }),\n]\n\n// v9\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\nconst columns: Array<ColumnDef<typeof features, Person>> = columnHelper.columns(\n  [\n    columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n      header: 'Age',\n      sortFn: 'alphanumeric',\n    }),\n  ],\n)\n```\n\nUse `columnHelper.columns([...])` for better inference across nested columns.\n\n---\n\n## Rendering Changes\n\nThe v9 `FlexRender` component supports shorthand props for cells, headers, and footers.\n\n```vue\n<!-- v8 -->\n<FlexRender :render=\"cell.column.columnDef.cell\" :props=\"cell.getContext()\" />\n\n<!-- v9 preferred -->\n<FlexRender :cell=\"cell\" />\n<FlexRender :header=\"header\" />\n<FlexRender :footer=\"footer\" />\n```\n\nThe older `:render` and `:props` shape still compiles, but the shorthand props are the preferred migration target.\n\n---\n\n## The `tableOptions()` Utility\n\n`tableOptions()` helps compose shared table option fragments.\n\n```ts\nimport { tableOptions } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst baseOptions = tableOptions({\n  features,\n  defaultColumn: {\n    minSize: 40,\n  },\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  ...baseOptions,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## `createTableHook`: Composable Table Patterns\n\n`createTableHook` creates shared Vue table helpers with features, row models, and registered components already bound.\n\n```ts\nimport { createTableHook } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst { useAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n})\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst table = useAppTable({\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\nSee the [Composable Tables Guide](./composable-tables) for full patterns.\n\n---\n\n## TypeScript Changes Summary\n\n### Type Generics\n\nUse `TFeatures` as the first generic:\n\n```ts\nColumnDef<typeof features, Person>\nColumn<typeof features, Person>\nRow<typeof features, Person>\nTable<typeof features, Person>\n```\n\n### Using `typeof features`\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n})\n\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\n```\n\n### Using `StockFeatures`\n\n```ts\nimport type { StockFeatures } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\ntype PersonColumn = ColumnDef<StockFeatures, Person>\n```\n\n### `TableMeta`/`ColumnMeta` Typing Changes\n\nNo more declaration merging required! (Although it still works if you want to keep using it)\n\nGlobal declaration merging works exactly like it did in v8. The only change you need to make is updating the generics shape: both interfaces now take `TFeatures` as the first type parameter.\n\n```ts\ndeclare module '@tanstack/vue-table' {\n  interface ColumnMeta<TFeatures, TData, TValue> {\n    align?: 'left' | 'right'\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThat's all that's required if you want to keep declaring meta types globally.\n\nOptionally, v9 also adds a new way to declare meta types **per-table** without declaration merging. You can use type-only `tableMeta`/`columnMeta` slots on the `features` option, which only affect tables created with that `features` object:\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<{ align?: 'left' | 'right' }>(),\n})\n```\n\nSee the new [Table and Column Meta Guide](../../../guide/table-and-column-meta) for full details on both approaches.\n\n### `FilterFns`/`SortFns`/`AggregationFns`/`FilterMeta` Augmentation Replaced by Registry Slots\n\nIn v8, making a custom function usable as a string reference (like `filterFn: 'fuzzy'`) required `declare module` augmentation of the `FilterFns` interface, and typing filter meta required augmenting `FilterMeta`. In v9, registering the function in the matching registry slot does both jobs with no global augmentation:\n\n```ts\n// v8\ndeclare module '@tanstack/vue-table' {\n  interface FilterFns {\n    fuzzy: FilterFn<unknown>\n  }\n  interface FilterMeta {\n    itemRank: RankingInfo\n  }\n}\n\n// v9 - register in the slot; the key becomes a valid string value\ninterface FuzzyFilterMeta {\n  itemRank?: RankingInfo\n}\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  filterFns: { fuzzy: fuzzyFilter },\n  filterMeta: metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>(),\n})\n\n// 'fuzzy' now typechecks in column defs for tables using these features\ncolumnHelper.accessor('name', { filterFn: 'fuzzy' })\n```\n\nThe same pattern applies to `sortFns` (for `sortFn` string values) and `aggregationFns` (for `aggregationFn` string values). See the [Fuzzy Filtering Guide](./fuzzy-filtering.md) for a complete example.\n\n### `RowData` Type Restriction\n\nPrefer explicit object row types:\n\n```ts\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Migration Checklist\n\n- [ ] Replace `useVueTable` with `useTable`.\n- [ ] Define `features` using `tableFeatures()` (or use `stockFeatures`)\n- [ ] Move row model factories into `tableFeatures` as slots (e.g. `filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel()`).\n- [ ] Remove `getCoreRowModel`; the core row model is automatic.\n- [ ] Move `sortFns`, `filterFns`, and `aggregationFns` into `tableFeatures` as slots (row model factories no longer take arguments).\n- [ ] Replace destructured row/cell/column/header methods with calls on the instance (for example, `row.getValue('name')`).\n- [ ] Replace `table.getState()` reads with `table.atoms.<slice>.get()` or `table.store.get()`.\n- [ ] Use Vue getters for controlled `state` slices.\n- [ ] Replace top-level `onStateChange` with per-slice callbacks or external atoms.\n- [ ] Rename `sortingFn` to `sortFn`.\n- [ ] Convert custom aggregation callables to `constructAggregationFn({ aggregate, merge? })` definitions.\n- [ ] Add `typeof features` to column helpers and types.\n- [ ] Replace `declare module` augmentation of `FilterFns`/`SortFns`/`AggregationFns` with registry-slot registration, and `FilterMeta` augmentation with the `filterMeta` slot.\n- [ ] Prefer `<FlexRender :cell=\"cell\" />`, `:header`, and `:footer` shorthand rendering.\n- [ ] Audit `stockFeatures` before production.\n\n---\n\n## Examples\n\n- [Basic useTable](../examples/basic-use-table)\n- [Basic External Atoms](../examples/basic-external-atoms)\n- [Basic External State](../examples/basic-external-state)\n- [With TanStack Query](../examples/with-tanstack-query)\n- [Sorting](../examples/sorting)\n- [Pagination](../examples/pagination)\n- [Composable Tables](../examples/composable-tables)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Migrating to TanStack Table V9 (Vue)\n---\n\n## What's New in TanStack Table V9\n\nTanStack Table V9 delivers major performance improvements, hundreds of bug fixes, new and refreshed features, and optional helpers for composing and managing tables. Despite the scale of the release, the headless model, core table logic, column definitions, and rendering patterns remain familiar. Here are the key changes:\n\n### 1. Better Performance\n\n- **Lower memory usage**: The core architecture now shares more behavior across table objects, with some large-table scenarios seeing up to 90% memory savings.\n- **Faster client-side row models**: Sorting, filtering, and aggregation paths have improved algorithms and memoization, with many scenarios seeing up to 40-70% speed improvements.\n- **Better column resizing performance**: The same architectural and memoization work also speeds up column resizing.\n\n### 2. State Management Overhaul\n\n- **TanStack Store foundation**: Table state is backed by TanStack Store atoms.\n- **Vue reactivity integration**: Table atoms are backed by Vue refs and computed values, and `useTable` unwraps reactive option values like `data`.\n- **Fine-grained subscriptions**: Registered features expose per-slice state through `table.atoms`, so reads can stay scoped to the state they need.\n\n### 3. Type-Safety Improvements\n\n- **New and revamped type helpers**: There are helpers for defining columns, custom filters, sorts, aggregations, column and table meta, shared table options and components, and more.\n- **Per-table meta types**: `tableMeta`, `columnMeta`, and `filterMeta` slots let you type meta for a specific table instead of globally augmenting shared interfaces. **No more global declaration merging required!**\n- **Feature-gated APIs**: APIs only exist when their feature is registered, and `tableFeatures()` validates feature prerequisites at the type level.\n\n### 4. Tree Shaking and Extensibility\n\n- **Import only the features you use**: Tables that only need sorting do not ship filtering, pagination, or other unused feature code.\n- **Tree-shakeable row models and functions**: Row model factories and `filterFns` / `sortFns` / `aggregationFns` now live on `tableFeatures()`, so unused processing code can be dropped.\n- **Custom features use the same system**: Your own feature plugins can register state, options, and APIs alongside the built-in features. See the [Custom Features Guide](./custom-features.md).\n\n### 5. Composability\n\n- **`tableOptions()`**: Compose reusable table configuration, including features, row models, and default options.\n- **`createTableHook()`**: Define shared Vue table factories with pre-bound features, row models, defaults, and components.\n\n### 6. New and Refreshed Features\n\n- **New Features**\n  - **Cell Selection**: `cellSelectionFeature` adds spreadsheet-style rectangular cell range selection, with drag, Shift-extend, and multiple disjoint ranges. See the [Cell Selection Guide](./cell-selection.md).\n  - **Cell Spanning**: `cellSpanningFeature` merges body cells across rows and columns (`spanRows` / `spanColumns`, with span-aware cell selection), and header groups now compute `header.rowSpan` so shallow columns can span header rows. See the [Cell Spanning Guide](./cell-spanning.md).\n- **Refreshed Features**\n  - **More capable features**: Aggregation, Row Selection, Column Pinning, and Column Resizing have all been made more feature rich (multiple aggregation definitions per column, Shift range selection, logical `start`/`end` pinning, and more).\n  - **New core APIs**: New table and row APIs (like `table.getMaxSubRowDepth()`, `row.getDisplayIndex()`) round out the core feature set.\n\n### 7. Modern Builds\n\n- **ESM-only**: UMD and CJS builds have been dropped. Packages ship as modern ESM.\n- **TypeScript target `ES2022`**: Compiled output now targets ES2022.\n- **Smaller install size**: Published packages no longer ship `src` or source maps, which reduces install footprint.\n\n### The Good News: Most Table Logic Is Still Familiar\n\n- Column definitions keep the same basic `accessorKey`, `accessorFn`, `header`, `cell`, and `footer` shapes.\n- Feature APIs like `table.nextPage()`, `column.toggleSorting()`, and `row.toggleSelected()` remain the preferred way to update state.\n- Templates still render header groups, rows, and cells from the table instance.\n\nThe main migration is replacing `useVueTable` with `useTable`, then moving feature and row-model setup into the v9 shape.\n\n---\n\n## Core Breaking Changes\n\n### Hook Rename\n\n```ts\n// v8\nimport { useVueTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable(options)\n\n// v9\nimport { useTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useTable(options)\n```\n\n### New Required `features` Table Option\n\nIn Table V9, you must explicitly declare which features your table uses. Features, Row Models, and Row Model processing \"Fns\" are defined on the new `features` table option.\n\n```ts\n// Table V8\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  sortingFns,\n  useVueTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable({\n  columns,\n  data,\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  sortingFns,\n})\n\n// Table V9\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n  useTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\n// All table options that concern including code modules (features, row models, Fns, etc.)\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature, // new - import and pass the feature you want to use\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(), // now row models are defined on the features object\n  sortFns, // now Fns are defined on the features object\n  // ...more features, row models, etc.\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features, // new required option\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\n`data` can be a raw array, a `ref`, a `computed`, or a getter. The adapter unwraps reactive option values and keeps the table synced.\n\n#### Shortcut: Use `stockFeatures` for Table V8-like Behavior\n\n`stockFeatures` is useful for early migration before you audit feature usage.\n\n```ts\nimport { stockFeatures, useTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features: stockFeatures,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\nUse it as a temporary migration shortcut. Explicit feature registration is the production target.\n\n### Available Features\n\n| Feature           | Import Name               |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Column Faceting   | `columnFacetingFeature`   |\n| Column Filtering  | `columnFilteringFeature`  |\n| Column Grouping   | `columnGroupingFeature`   |\n| Column Ordering   | `columnOrderingFeature`   |\n| Column Pinning    | `columnPinningFeature`    |\n| Column Resizing   | `columnResizingFeature`   |\n| Column Sizing     | `columnSizingFeature`     |\n| Column Visibility | `columnVisibilityFeature` |\n| Global Filtering  | `globalFilteringFeature`  |\n| Row Aggregation   | `rowAggregationFeature`   |\n| Row Expanding     | `rowExpandingFeature`     |\n| Row Pagination    | `rowPaginationFeature`    |\n| Row Pinning       | `rowPinningFeature`       |\n| Row Selection     | `rowSelectionFeature`     |\n| Row Sorting       | `rowSortingFeature`       |\n\n### Row Model Factories\n\nRow model factories now live on the `features` object (passed to `tableFeatures`). The `rowModels` option has been removed. Function registries (`filterFns`, `sortFns`, `aggregationFns`) are also slots on the features object. Row model slots are type-checked, so each row model must be specified after its associated feature in the same `tableFeatures` call.\n\n#### Migration Mapping\n\n| Table V8 Option            | Table V9 `tableFeatures` Slot | Table V9 Factory Function     |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `getCoreRowModel()`        | (automatic)                   | Not needed, always included   |\n| `getFilteredRowModel()`    | `filteredRowModel`            | `createFilteredRowModel()`    |\n| `getSortedRowModel()`      | `sortedRowModel`              | `createSortedRowModel()`      |\n| `getPaginationRowModel()`  | `paginatedRowModel`           | `createPaginatedRowModel()`   |\n| `getExpandedRowModel()`    | `expandedRowModel`            | `createExpandedRowModel()`    |\n| `getGroupedRowModel()`     | `groupedRowModel`             | `createGroupedRowModel()`     |\n| `getFacetedRowModel()`     | `facetedRowModel`             | `createFacetedRowModel()`     |\n| `getFacetedMinMaxValues()` | `facetedMinMaxValues`         | `createFacetedMinMaxValues()` |\n| `getFacetedUniqueValues()` | `facetedUniqueValues`         | `createFacetedUniqueValues()` |\n\n#### Full Migration Example\n\n```ts\n// v8\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortingFns,\n  useVueTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable({\n  columns,\n  data,\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortingFns,\n})\n\n// v9\nimport {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n  useTable,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\n#### Prefer Individual Fn Imports Over Full Registries\n\nThe `filterFns`, `sortFns`, and `aggregationFns` registry exports are now deprecated in favor of importing individual `filterFn_*`, `sortFn_*`, and `aggregationFn_*` functions and registering only the ones you use (or passing functions directly in column definitions with no registration at all). The full registries still work, but spreading them puts every built-in function in your bundle. String names, including the default `'auto'`, only resolve functions you have registered.\n\n```ts\n// Before: registers every built-in function\nimport { filterFns, sortFns } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\n// After: registers only the functions you use\nimport {\n  filterFn_includesString,\n  sortFn_alphanumeric,\n  sortFn_text,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns: { includesString: filterFn_includesString },\n  sortFns: { alphanumeric: sortFn_alphanumeric, text: sortFn_text },\n})\n```\n\n### Instance Methods Must Be Called on Their Instance\n\nIn v9, methods on rows, cells, columns, headers, and similar table objects are shared on the object's prototype instead of being created as arrow functions on each object. This improves memory usage, but it means destructuring those methods loses the `this` context they need to operate on the instance.\n\n```ts\n// v8 - worked because getValue closed over the row object\nconst { getValue } = row\nconst value = getValue('name')\n\n// v9 - call the method on the instance\nconst value = row.getValue('name')\n```\n\nThis applies to row, cell, column, header, and related instance APIs, but not to the table instance itself. Audit code that destructures methods from table objects or passes them around as bare callbacks. Prefer calling them through the original object, for example `row.getValue('name')`, `cell.getContext()`, `column.getCanSort()`, or `header.getContext()`.\n\nBecause these methods now live on the prototype, they also do not appear as own properties in `Object.keys(instance)`, object spread, or `JSON.stringify`. A shallow clone like `{ ...row }` copies row data but does not copy row methods. The methods are still callable normally because JavaScript looks them up through the prototype chain.\n\n---\n\n## State Management Changes\n\nVue v9 table state is atom-backed and Vue-aware. Prefer Vue `computed` values around narrow atom reads over broad whole-state reads.\n\n| Surface                     | Use                                                                                           |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `table.atoms.<slice>.get()` | Narrow reactive reads inside Vue tracking scopes.                                             |\n| `table.store.get()`         | Current full state snapshot. Use mostly for debug output or intentionally broad dependencies. |\n| `table.Subscribe`           | Deprecated compatibility wrapper. Read table APIs or atoms in native Vue reactive contexts.   |\n| `table.baseAtoms.<slice>`   | Internal writable atoms. Prefer feature APIs or external atoms.                               |\n\n### Accessing State\n\n```ts\n// v8\nconst sorting = table.getState().sorting\n\n// v9: narrow atom read\nconst sorting = table.atoms.sorting.get()\n\n// v9: full snapshot\nconst tableState = table.store.get()\n```\n\nUse Vue primitives to derive reactive values:\n\n```ts\nimport { computed } from 'vue'\n\nconst pagination = computed(() => table.atoms.pagination.get())\nconst pageIndex = computed(() => pagination.value.pageIndex)\nconst tableStateJson = computed(() =>\n  JSON.stringify(table.store.get(), null, 2),\n)\n```\n\n### Reactive Options\n\n`data` can be a `ref` or `computed`; the adapter unwraps and syncs it.\n\n```ts\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\n\nconst data = ref(makeData(100))\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n\ndata.value = makeData(200)\n```\n\nGetter-based options also work:\n\n```ts\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data.value\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Replace `table.Subscribe`\n\n`table.Subscribe` is deprecated. It only passes `table.atoms` to its child function and adds no subscription logic. Read table APIs or atoms directly inside templates, render functions, computed values, or watcher sources.\n\nFor example, return this JSX from a component's render function:\n\n```tsx\n<span>Page {table.atoms.pagination.get().pageIndex + 1}</span>\n```\n\nIf you used `table.Subscribe` as a component to isolate rendering, move those reads into a child component. Calling `table.Subscribe` as a plain function never created a separate component render boundary.\n\n### Controlled State\n\nThe v8-style `state` + `on[State]Change` controlled state patterns still work and remain convenient for simple integrations. For new v9 code, prefer owning state slices with external atoms (see [External Atoms](#external-atoms) below), which give you fine-grained subscriptions without mirroring state through Vue refs.\n\nWhen Vue refs own a state slice, expose the current value with getters and update the ref in the matching callback.\n\n```ts\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport type {\n  PaginationState,\n  SortingState,\n  Updater,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nfunction resolveUpdater<T>(updater: Updater<T>, previous: T): T {\n  return typeof updater === 'function'\n    ? (updater as (old: T) => T)(previous)\n    : updater\n}\n\nconst sorting = ref<SortingState>([])\nconst pagination = ref<PaginationState>({\n  pageIndex: 0,\n  pageSize: 10,\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data.value\n  },\n  state: {\n    get sorting() {\n      return sorting.value\n    },\n    get pagination() {\n      return pagination.value\n    },\n  },\n  onSortingChange: (updater) => {\n    sorting.value = resolveUpdater(updater, sorting.value)\n  },\n  onPaginationChange: (updater) => {\n    pagination.value = resolveUpdater(updater, pagination.value)\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe v8-style top-level `onStateChange` callback is gone. Use per-slice callbacks or external atoms.\n\nIf you want to lift or listen to any state change, set up a subscription to the `table.store`:\n\n```ts\nconst unsubscribe = table.store.subscribe((state) => {\n  console.log(state)\n})\n```\n\n### External Atoms\n\nUse external atoms when the app should own and share state slices outside the table.\n\n```ts\nimport { createAtom, useSelector } from '@tanstack/vue-store'\nimport type { PaginationState, SortingState } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst sortingAtom = createAtom<SortingState>([])\nconst paginationAtom = createAtom<PaginationState>({\n  pageIndex: 0,\n  pageSize: 10,\n})\n\nconst pagination = useSelector(paginationAtom)\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data.value\n  },\n  atoms: {\n    sorting: sortingAtom,\n    pagination: paginationAtom,\n  },\n})\n\npagination.value.pageIndex\n```\n\nDo not provide both `atoms.pagination` and `state.pagination`; the atom owns that slice.\n\n---\n\n## Feature-by-Feature Breaking Changes\n\n### Sorting\n\n| v8                   | v9                |\n| -------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `sortingFn`          | `sortFn`          |\n| `sortingFns`         | `sortFns`         |\n| `getSortingFn()`     | `getSortFn()`     |\n| `getAutoSortingFn()` | `getAutoSortFn()` |\n| `SortingFn`          | `SortFn`          |\n\n### Column Pinning\n\nV9 changes column pinning to use logical `start`/`end` terminology instead of the physical `left`/`right` terminology used in V8. In LTR languages/layouts, `start` usually corresponds to left and `end` to right; in RTL languages/layouts, `start` usually corresponds to right and `end` to left. There are no deprecated aliases.\n\n| V8                                   | V9                                   |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `columnPinning.left`                 | `columnPinning.start`                |\n| `columnPinning.right`                | `columnPinning.end`                  |\n| `column.pin('left')`                 | `column.pin('start')`                |\n| `column.pin('right')`                | `column.pin('end')`                  |\n| `column.getIsPinned() === 'left'`    | `column.getIsPinned() === 'start'`   |\n| `column.getIsPinned() === 'right'`   | `column.getIsPinned() === 'end'`     |\n| `row.getLeftVisibleCells()`          | `row.getStartVisibleCells()`         |\n| `row.getRightVisibleCells()`         | `row.getEndVisibleCells()`           |\n| `table.getLeftHeaderGroups()`        | `table.getStartHeaderGroups()`       |\n| `table.getRightHeaderGroups()`       | `table.getEndHeaderGroups()`         |\n| `table.getLeftLeafColumns()`         | `table.getStartLeafColumns()`        |\n| `table.getRightLeafColumns()`        | `table.getEndLeafColumns()`          |\n| `table.getLeftVisibleLeafColumns()`  | `table.getStartVisibleLeafColumns()` |\n| `table.getRightVisibleLeafColumns()` | `table.getEndVisibleLeafColumns()`   |\n| `table.getLeftTotalSize()`           | `table.getStartTotalSize()`          |\n| `table.getRightTotalSize()`          | `table.getEndTotalSize()`            |\n| `column.getStart('left')`            | `column.getStart('start')`           |\n| `column.getAfter('right')`           | `column.getAfter('end')`             |\n| `column.getIndex('left')`            | `column.getIndex('start')`           |\n| `column.getIndex('right')`           | `column.getIndex('end')`             |\n\nThis rename is about logical table regions, not automatic DOM direction handling. For sticky column pinning, prefer CSS logical properties like `insetInlineStart` and `insetInlineEnd`. The `columnResizeDirection` table option is unchanged.\n\nThe table-level `enablePinning` option has also been split into separate options:\n\n```ts\nenableColumnPinning: true\nenableRowPinning: true\n```\n\n### Column Sizing vs. Column Resizing Split\n\nColumn resizing now has its own feature and state slice.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnSizingFeature,\n  columnResizingFeature,\n})\n```\n\n`columnSizingInfo` became `columnResizing`, `setColumnSizingInfo()` became `setColumnResizing()`, and `onColumnSizingInfoChange` became `onColumnResizingChange`.\n\n### Grouping and Aggregation\n\nAggregation is now its own feature, independent from column grouping. `stockFeatures` still includes both, so tables using it need no feature-registration change. If you declare features explicitly, add `rowAggregationFeature` whenever columns use `aggregationFn`, `aggregatedCell`, `getAggregationValue`, or `cell.getIsAggregated`. Add `columnGroupingFeature` and `groupedRowModel` only when you also group rows.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature, // only for grouped rows\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  aggregationFns: { sum: aggregationFn_sum },\n})\n```\n\nCustom aggregation callables have changed to context-based definitions:\n\n```ts\n// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\nconst total = (columnId, leafRows, childRows) =>\n  leafRows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + row.getValue(columnId), 0)\n\n// Current V9\nconst total = constructAggregationFn({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + Number(getValue(row)), 0),\n})\n```\n\nThe old per-function choice between `childRows` and `leafRows` is replaced by a single depth-selected `context.rows`, controlled by the `maxAggregationDepth` column option. The default (`0`) preserves V8's direct-child grouped aggregation; use `Infinity` to aggregate terminal leaf rows.\n\n`column.getAggregationValue()` now takes a single options object instead of positional arguments:\n\n```ts\n// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\ncolumn.getAggregationValue(rows, maxDepth)\n\n// Current V9\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows, maxDepth })\n```\n\n`column.getAggregationFn()` is now `column.getAggregationFns()` because a column can run multiple definitions, and the old callable `AggregationFn`/`CreatedAggregationFn` types are replaced by `AggregationFnDef`.\n\nSee the [Grouping Guide](./grouping) and the [Aggregation Guide](./aggregation) for full documentation of the new capabilities.\n\n### Row Selection\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Minor breaking change:** `row.getToggleSelectedHandler()` now enables inclusive Shift range selection by default when `rowSelectionFeature` is enabled. Existing checkboxes or rows wired through this handler establish an anchor on an ordinary interaction and select or deselect the current display-order range on a Shift interaction. Direct `row.toggleSelected()` calls are unchanged.\n>\n> Set `enableRowRangeSelection: false` to preserve the previous non-range handler behavior. The handler must receive an event that exposes Shift directly or through `nativeEvent`; see [Shift Range Selection](./row-selection.md#shift-range-selection).\n\nThe \"some rows selected\" checks were simplified to mean \"at least one row is selected\":\n\n| API                                 | v8                                                  | v9                                            |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `table.getIsSomeRowsSelected()`     | `true` when some but not all rows are selected      | `true` when at least one row is selected      |\n| `table.getIsSomePageRowsSelected()` | `true` when some but not all page rows are selected | `true` when at least one page row is selected |\n\nIn v8 these returned `false` once every row was selected; in v9 they stay `true`. If you use them to drive an indeterminate \"select all\" checkbox, gate the indeterminate state on the matching all-selected check so it clears at full selection:\n\n`getIsSomeRowsSelected() && !getIsAllRowsSelected()`\n\n### Row and Internal API Changes\n\nSome row APIs have changed from private to public:\n\n| Table V8                                 | Table V9                               |\n| ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `row._getAllCellsByColumnId()` (private) | `row.getAllCellsByColumnId()` (public) |\n\nAll other internal APIs prefixed with `_` have been removed. If you were using any of these, use their public equivalents:\n\n- Removed: `table._getPinnedRows()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedRowModel()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedMinMaxValues()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedUniqueValues()`\n\n---\n\n## Column Helper Changes\n\nColumn helpers and column types now include `TFeatures` first.\n\n```ts\n// v8\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<Person>()\nconst columns: ColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    sortingFn: 'alphanumeric',\n  }),\n]\n\n// v9\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\nconst columns: Array<ColumnDef<typeof features, Person>> = columnHelper.columns(\n  [\n    columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n      header: 'Age',\n      sortFn: 'alphanumeric',\n    }),\n  ],\n)\n```\n\nUse `columnHelper.columns([...])` for better inference across nested columns.\n\n---\n\n## Rendering Changes\n\nThe v9 `FlexRender` component supports shorthand props for cells, headers, and footers.\n\n```vue\n<!-- v8 -->\n<FlexRender :render=\"cell.column.columnDef.cell\" :props=\"cell.getContext()\" />\n\n<!-- v9 preferred -->\n<FlexRender :cell=\"cell\" />\n<FlexRender :header=\"header\" />\n<FlexRender :footer=\"footer\" />\n```\n\nThe older `:render` and `:props` shape still compiles, but the shorthand props are the preferred migration target.\n\n---\n\n## The `tableOptions()` Utility\n\n`tableOptions()` helps compose shared table option fragments.\n\n```ts\nimport { tableOptions } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst baseOptions = tableOptions({\n  features,\n  defaultColumn: {\n    minSize: 40,\n  },\n})\n\nconst table = useTable({\n  ...baseOptions,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## `createTableHook`: Composable Table Patterns\n\n`createTableHook` creates shared Vue table helpers with features, row models, and registered components already bound.\n\n```ts\nimport { createTableHook } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst { useAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n})\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst table = useAppTable({\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\nSee the [Composable Tables Guide](./composable-tables) for full patterns.\n\n---\n\n## TypeScript Changes Summary\n\n### Type Generics\n\nUse `TFeatures` as the first generic:\n\n```ts\nColumnDef<typeof features, Person>\nColumn<typeof features, Person>\nRow<typeof features, Person>\nTable<typeof features, Person>\n```\n\n### Using `typeof features`\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n})\n\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\n```\n\n### Using `StockFeatures`\n\n```ts\nimport type { StockFeatures } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\ntype PersonColumn = ColumnDef<StockFeatures, Person>\n```\n\n### `TableMeta`/`ColumnMeta` Typing Changes\n\nNo more declaration merging required! (Although it still works if you want to keep using it)\n\nGlobal declaration merging works exactly like it did in v8. The only change you need to make is updating the generics shape: both interfaces now take `TFeatures` as the first type parameter.\n\n```ts\ndeclare module '@tanstack/vue-table' {\n  interface ColumnMeta<TFeatures, TData, TValue> {\n    align?: 'left' | 'right'\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThat's all that's required if you want to keep declaring meta types globally.\n\nOptionally, v9 also adds a new way to declare meta types **per-table** without declaration merging. You can use type-only `tableMeta`/`columnMeta` slots on the `features` option, which only affect tables created with that `features` object:\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<{ align?: 'left' | 'right' }>(),\n})\n```\n\nSee the new [Table and Column Meta Guide](../../../guide/table-and-column-meta) for full details on both approaches.\n\n### `FilterFns`/`SortFns`/`AggregationFns`/`FilterMeta` Augmentation Replaced by Registry Slots\n\nIn v8, making a custom function usable as a string reference (like `filterFn: 'fuzzy'`) required `declare module` augmentation of the `FilterFns` interface, and typing filter meta required augmenting `FilterMeta`. In v9, registering the function in the matching registry slot does both jobs with no global augmentation:\n\n```ts\n// v8\ndeclare module '@tanstack/vue-table' {\n  interface FilterFns {\n    fuzzy: FilterFn<unknown>\n  }\n  interface FilterMeta {\n    itemRank: RankingInfo\n  }\n}\n\n// v9 - register in the slot; the key becomes a valid string value\ninterface FuzzyFilterMeta {\n  itemRank?: RankingInfo\n}\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  filterFns: { fuzzy: fuzzyFilter },\n  filterMeta: metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>(),\n})\n\n// 'fuzzy' now typechecks in column defs for tables using these features\ncolumnHelper.accessor('name', { filterFn: 'fuzzy' })\n```\n\nThe same pattern applies to `sortFns` (for `sortFn` string values) and `aggregationFns` (for `aggregationFn` string values). See the [Fuzzy Filtering Guide](./fuzzy-filtering.md) for a complete example.\n\n### `RowData` Type Restriction\n\nPrefer explicit object row types:\n\n```ts\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Migration Checklist\n\n- [ ] Replace `useVueTable` with `useTable`.\n- [ ] Define `features` using `tableFeatures()` (or use `stockFeatures`)\n- [ ] Move row model factories into `tableFeatures` as slots (e.g. `filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel()`).\n- [ ] Remove `getCoreRowModel`; the core row model is automatic.\n- [ ] Move `sortFns`, `filterFns`, and `aggregationFns` into `tableFeatures` as slots (row model factories no longer take arguments).\n- [ ] Replace destructured row/cell/column/header methods with calls on the instance (for example, `row.getValue('name')`).\n- [ ] Replace `table.getState()` reads with `table.atoms.<slice>.get()` or `table.store.get()`.\n- [ ] Use Vue getters for controlled `state` slices.\n- [ ] Replace top-level `onStateChange` with per-slice callbacks or external atoms.\n- [ ] Rename `sortingFn` to `sortFn`.\n- [ ] Convert custom aggregation callables to `constructAggregationFn({ aggregate, merge? })` definitions.\n- [ ] Add `typeof features` to column helpers and types.\n- [ ] Replace `declare module` augmentation of `FilterFns`/`SortFns`/`AggregationFns` with registry-slot registration, and `FilterMeta` augmentation with the `filterMeta` slot.\n- [ ] Prefer `<FlexRender :cell=\"cell\" />`, `:header`, and `:footer` shorthand rendering.\n- [ ] Audit `stockFeatures` before production.\n\n---\n\n## Examples\n\n- [Basic useTable](../examples/basic-use-table)\n- [Basic External Atoms](../examples/basic-external-atoms)\n- [Basic External State](../examples/basic-external-state)\n- [With TanStack Query](../examples/with-tanstack-query)\n- [Sorting](../examples/sorting)\n- [Pagination](../examples/pagination)\n- [Composable Tables](../examples/composable-tables)\n"}
